{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734190",
      "title": "How Authentication Works",
      "sourceHash": "4cb72890bd2cceb535b7f9f02cdbab01b7477887daf7782eff39190c94a99f8f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "Now for this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "I have a demo project prepared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 8.91,
          "en": "and that is actually the project we also used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.91,
          "end": 10.29,
          "en": "in the routing section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.29,
          "end": 14.31,
          "en": "with some extra features especially the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.31,
          "end": 15.78,
          "en": "which I'm providing for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.78,
          "end": 19.62,
          "en": "This dummy backend API, learn some new tricks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.62,
          "end": 22.26,
          "en": "and does now enforce user authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 24.963,
          "en": "and support user creation and login.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.83,
          "end": 28.92,
          "en": "And before we start writing some code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.92,
          "end": 31.05,
          "en": "and before we dive into this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.05,
          "end": 33.03,
          "en": "it is of course important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.03,
          "end": 35.97,
          "en": "how authentication actually works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.97,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "in React apps and what it actually means.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 40.83,
          "en": "Now let's start by clarifying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.83,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "what exactly authentication means.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 47.04,
          "en": "In the end it means that certain resources,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.04,
          "end": 51.09,
          "en": "certain backend routes, for example, should be protected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.09,
          "end": 54.27,
          "en": "and should not be accessible by everyone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.27,
          "end": 58.32,
          "en": "So the front end application, the React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.32,
          "end": 61.92,
          "en": "that wants to access certain backend resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.92,
          "end": 65.37,
          "en": "must authenticate before this access is granted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.37,
          "end": 66.903,
          "en": "It must get permission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.95,
          "end": 69.06,
          "en": "And for that of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.06,
          "end": 73.11,
          "en": "the question is how does our client side React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.11,
          "end": 75.75,
          "en": "get permission from that backend application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.75,
          "end": 76.863,
          "en": "running on a server?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.78999999999999,
          "end": 80.61,
          "en": "Well, it all starts with sending a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.61,
          "end": 82.14,
          "en": "with user credentials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.14,
          "end": 85.17,
          "en": "So with an email and a password, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.17,
          "end": 87.63,
          "en": "to that back and server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.63,
          "end": 88.86,
          "en": "That backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.86,
          "end": 91.83,
          "en": "is then able to validate those credentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.83,
          "end": 95.19,
          "en": "or create a new user if that's what we're doing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.19,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "And then if the credentials are valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 101.67,
          "en": "if we did provide a valid email password combination",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.67,
          "end": 104.37,
          "en": "then the server will send us back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 107.25,
          "en": "that basically gives us permission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.25,
          "end": 110.91,
          "en": "to access certain protected resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.91,
          "end": 112.86,
          "en": "But how does this response look like?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.86,
          "end": 114.53999999999999,
          "en": "Is it a simple yes or no?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.53999999999999,
          "end": 115.95,
          "en": "Yes, you have access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 115.95,
          "end": 117.39,
          "en": "No, you don't have access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 117.39,
          "end": 118.443,
          "en": "Is that enough?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 119.31,
          "end": 122.76,
          "en": "Well, the answer is a yes alone would not be enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 122.76,
          "end": 125.73,
          "en": "because if a server responds with a yes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 125.73,
          "end": 129.42,
          "en": "and in future requests from the client to the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 129.42,
          "end": 132.42,
          "en": "we then simply append that information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 132.42,
          "end": 134.55,
          "en": "that we got a yes in the past.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.55,
          "end": 135.93,
          "en": "That of course is not enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 135.93,
          "end": 137.97,
          "en": "because we could simply fake that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 137.97,
          "end": 141.24,
          "en": "We could simply say that we have permission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.24,
          "end": 144.51,
          "en": "so the server must reply with something else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.51,
          "end": 145.92000000000002,
          "en": "than a yes or no,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 145.92000000000002,
          "end": 148.53,
          "en": "something that can be validated on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 148.53,
          "end": 151.11,
          "en": "and that proves that we really got permission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 151.11,
          "end": 153.72,
          "en": "from the server in the past.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 153.72,
          "end": 156.6,
          "en": "So therefore we can't just save",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 156.6,
          "end": 159.72,
          "en": "and use a yes answer after logging in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 159.72,
          "end": 163.2,
          "en": "We can't just attach a yes to future requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 163.2,
          "end": 165.69,
          "en": "that want to access protected resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 165.69,
          "end": 167.94,
          "en": "because we could fake that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 167.94,
          "end": 170.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now, there are two main solutions for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 170.57999999999998,
          "end": 175.23,
          "en": "We could use server side sessions or authentication tokens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 175.23,
          "end": 178.89,
          "en": "Now, server side sessions are a very popular solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 178.89,
          "end": 181.68,
          "en": "especially for full stack applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 181.68,
          "end": 185.13,
          "en": "where you don't have a decoupled front end and back end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 185.13,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "as we do often have it with React though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 190.53,
          "en": "So it's not ideal for React as you will learn.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 190.53,
          "end": 192.96,
          "en": "But the idea behind server side sessions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 192.96,
          "end": 194.91,
          "en": "would be that on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 194.91,
          "end": 197.94,
          "en": "after a user was logged in and authenticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 197.94,
          "end": 200.79,
          "en": "we store a unique identifier on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 200.79,
          "end": 203.82,
          "en": "We basically stored a yes on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 203.82,
          "end": 207.87,
          "en": "and mapped that to a specific client with help of an id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 207.87,
          "end": 209.823,
          "en": "that's then sent back to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 210.66,
          "end": 214.44,
          "en": "And the client then sends that ID with future requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 214.44,
          "end": 217.53,
          "en": "which do try to access protected resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 217.53,
          "end": 221.76,
          "en": "And since we stored a yes mapped to that idea on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 221.76,
          "end": 223.53,
          "en": "the server is able to check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 223.53,
          "end": 226.41,
          "en": "whether that client really does have permission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 226.41,
          "end": 229.07999999999998,
          "en": "to access protected resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 229.07999999999998,
          "end": 231.6,
          "en": "Now, server side sessions are a great way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 231.6,
          "end": 236.43,
          "en": "of solving authentication or of enabling authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 236.43,
          "end": 239.1,
          "en": "but they do require a tight coupling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 239.1,
          "end": 240.99,
          "en": "between backend and frontend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 240.99,
          "end": 245.28,
          "en": "because the backend must store information about the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 245.28,
          "end": 246.81,
          "en": "And with React apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 246.81,
          "end": 250.89,
          "en": "you are often talking to decoupled backend APIs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 250.89,
          "end": 253.41,
          "en": "which are not closely coupled to a client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 253.41,
          "end": 256.5,
          "en": "and which don't store any client site information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 256.5,
          "end": 259.59,
          "en": "And that's where authentication tokens come into play.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 259.59,
          "end": 261.33,
          "en": "And that is indeed the mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 261.33,
          "end": 265.11,
          "en": "we will implement in this course section here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 265.11,
          "end": 267.93,
          "en": "The idea behind authentication tokens is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 267.93,
          "end": 272.25,
          "en": "that on the server after a user was authenticated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 272.25,
          "end": 276.06,
          "en": "so after a user sent a valid pair of credentials,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 276.06,
          "end": 281.06,
          "en": "for example, we create but don't store a permission token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 281.31,
          "end": 283.44,
          "en": "which is basically a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 283.44,
          "end": 285.96,
          "en": "that is created according to some algorithm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 285.96,
          "end": 289.26,
          "en": "and that includes some information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 289.26,
          "end": 291.75,
          "en": "So we create such a token on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 291.75,
          "end": 295.11,
          "en": "and we send that token back to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 295.11,
          "end": 297.96,
          "en": "Now, the special thing about that token is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 297.96,
          "end": 300.87,
          "en": "that it's validity can only be checked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 300.87,
          "end": 305.01,
          "en": "and proven by the backend that created that token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 305.01,
          "end": 308.25,
          "en": "because the token is created with help of some private key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 308.25,
          "end": 311.04,
          "en": "which is only known by the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 311.04,
          "end": 314.82,
          "en": "So in future requests from the client to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 314.82,
          "end": 317.64,
          "en": "we attach that token to those requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 317.64,
          "end": 320.7,
          "en": "and the backend is able to take a look at that token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 320.7,
          "end": 323.13,
          "en": "validated and see if it is a token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 323.13,
          "end": 325.74,
          "en": "that was created by that backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 325.74,
          "end": 327.51,
          "en": "And if it is a valid token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 327.51,
          "end": 331.8,
          "en": "then permission to those protected resources is granted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 331.8,
          "end": 334.68,
          "en": "And that is exactly what this dummy backend API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 334.68,
          "end": 337.92,
          "en": "which I'm providing to you here does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 337.92,
          "end": 340.56,
          "en": "In this dummy backend API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 340.56,
          "end": 343.71,
          "en": "When a user signs up or logs in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 343.71,
          "end": 348.12,
          "en": "what I'm doing in the end is I'm creating such a Jason token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 348.12,
          "end": 351.48,
          "en": "as it's called a Jason Web Token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 351.48,
          "end": 353.85,
          "en": "Now that token is created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 353.85,
          "end": 356.4,
          "en": "with help of a third party package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 356.4,
          "end": 358.44,
          "en": "and it's a very simple piece of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 358.44,
          "end": 359.64,
          "en": "that I'm executing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 359.64,
          "end": 362.31,
          "en": "Under the hood I'm using that third party package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 362.31,
          "end": 363.78,
          "en": "for creating a token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 363.78,
          "end": 366.12,
          "en": "that is created with help of a private key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 366.12,
          "end": 369.12,
          "en": "that's only known by the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 369.12,
          "end": 372.6,
          "en": "Of course, in reality, you would have a safer key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 372.6,
          "end": 374.04,
          "en": "than that simple key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 374.04,
          "end": 376.98,
          "en": "and you would probably not include it in your code base,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 376.98,
          "end": 378.66,
          "en": "but this is just a dummy backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 378.66,
          "end": 380.91,
          "en": "which we're using as a demo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 380.91,
          "end": 382.71,
          "en": "So here I'm creating such a token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 382.71,
          "end": 386.13,
          "en": "and again, that token is in the end just some string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 386.13,
          "end": 388.53,
